        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.669,
            0.807,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Some sums appear always no matter which 4 consecutive numbers are chosen. Isn’t that interesting?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.71,
            0.807,
            0.751
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Do these patterns occur no matter which 4 consecutive numbers are chosen? Is there a way to find out through reasoning?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.752,
            0.806,
            0.774
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hint:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Use algebra and describe the 8 expressions in a general form."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.779,
            0.848,
            0.854
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You might have noticed that the results of all expressions are even numbers. Even numbers have a factor of 2. Negative numbers having a factor 2 are also even numbers, for example, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "- 2 , - 4 , - 6 ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and so on. Check if anyone in your class got an odd number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.853,
            0.848,
            0.911
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When 4 consecutive numbers are chosen, no matter how the ‘+’ and ‘–’ signs are placed between them, the resulting expressions always have even parity."
            }
          ]
        },
